1817 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Vacutainer tube holder: The holder for vacuum blood collection is a plastic sleeve into which the phlebotomist screws the double-pointed needle.)
/K [15]
/P 6113 0 R
/Pg 26 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
1818 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Vacuum collection tubes: Vacuum collection tubes are glass or plastic tubes sealed with a partial vacuum inside by rubber stoppers. The air pressure inside the tube is negative, less than the normal environment. After inserting the long end of the needle into the vein, the phlebotomist pushes the tube into the holder so that the short end needle pierces the stopper. The difference in pressure between the inside of the tube and the vein causes blood to fill the tube. )
/K [16]
/P 6114 0 R
/Pg 26 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
