/Alt ()
/E (Use a winged steel needle, preferably 23 or 23 gauge, with an extension tube \(a butterfly\):)
/K [16]
/P 6232 0 R
/Pg 39 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
2144 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (avoid gauges of 25 or more because these may be associated with an increased risk of haemolysis;)
/K [17]
/P 6233 0 R
/Pg 39 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
2145 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (use a butterfly with either a syringe or an evacuated tube with an adaptor; a butterfly can provide easier access and movement, but movement of the attached syringe may make it difficult to draw blood.)
/K [18]
/P 6234 0 R
/Pg 39 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
