/Alt ()
/E (Immediately mix by inverting the tube gentlyno less than eight \(8\) times and no more than ten \(10\) times. Less than five inversions will result in incomplete clotting and incomplete separation of red cells from serum. Hemolysis of even a small number of red cells remaining above the gel in contact with serum will spuriously elevate results of tests, such as serum potassium and LD.)
/K [15]
/P 6338 0 R
/Pg 55 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
2592 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Do not remove the stopper at any time. Do not centrifuge immediately after drawing blood. Allow the blood to clot in an upright position for at least 30 minutes,but not longer than 1 hour before centrifugation.)
/K [16]
/P 6339 0 R
/Pg 55 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
