/Alt ()
/E (Do not use Serum Separator Tubes \(SSTs\) for therapeutic drug monitoring, LC/MS/MS or toxicological analysis. The polyester in the separator gel can extract lipophilic substances \(most drugs\), and can cause a falsely low drug concentration result. Instead, collect the specimen in a red-top tube containing no gel. Collect and process as described above and after centrifugation, transfer the serum with a pipette to a properly labeled plastic vial. Serum should be clear and free of red cells.)
/K [11]
/Pg 56 0 R
/S /H4
/T (Do not use Serum Separator Tubes \(SSTs\) for therapeutic drug monitoring, LC/MS/MS or toxicological analysis. The polyester in the separator gel can extract lipophilic substances \(most drugs\), and can cause a falsely low drug concentration result. Instead, collect the specimen in a red-top tube containing no gel. Collect and process as described above and after centrifugation, transfer the serum with a pipette to a properly labeled plastic vial. Serum should be clear and free of red cells.)
/Type /StructElem
>>
