<<
/Alt ()
/E (Policy for disposal of samples:)
/K [11]
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /H5
/T (Policy for disposal of samples:)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3772 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Beyond the defined retention time, the samples are discarded according to the BMW / Pollution Control Board guidelines.)
/K [12]
/P 6927 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3773 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Based on their specific tests, TRUSTlab has defined specific sample retention time.)
/K [13]
/P 6928 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3774 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (It is the responsibility of the concerned laboratory technician to discard the samples after the completion of the retention time.)
/K [14]
/P 6929 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3775 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (If indicated the samples may be preserved beyond their defined retention time for academic, research or medico-legal purposes.)
/K [15]
/P 6930 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3776 0 obj
<<
/E (HANDLING OF WASTES)
/K [23]
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /H2
/T (HANDLING OF WASTES)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3777 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (The segregation of wastes is done at the source of generation into yellow, red and blue bags.)
/K [17]
/P 6931 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3778 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Yellow bags are designated for infectious, non-sharp \(pathological and anatomical\) waste, including items contaminated with blood or body fluids, soiled bandages, dressings, cotton swabs, blood bags, transfusion sets \(non-PVC\), body tissues, body parts, and untreated microbiology and biotechnology waste.)
/K [18]
/P 6932 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3779 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (The red bags are meant for infected plastics like oxygen masks, gloves, syringes etc. for sterilization and shredding. These items should not be sent for incineration.)
/K [19]
/P 6933 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3780 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (The red and yellow bags and the sharp cans should be tied, autoclaved & then labeled and handed over to the biomedical waste collection agency. Records of biomedical waste are to be maintained.)
/K [20]
/P 6934 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3781 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Blue boxes are puncture proof containers for discarding whole and broken glassware. A biohazard symbol is displayed on them.)
/K [21]
/P 6935 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3782 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Needles used for blood collection are destroyed using a needle destroyer, while other sharp items, such as scalpel blades, are disinfected and safely discarded in designated sharp containers to prevent injury and contamination. The sharps should not be left lying even for a few minutes.)
/K [22]
/P 6936 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
3783 0 obj
<<
/K [24]
/P 1203 0 R
/Pg 89 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
