/Alt ()
/E (Anything received in 10% neutral buffered formalin can be held at room temperature until grossed by the resident. Refrigeration \(2-80C\) is not needed and should be avoided so as not to slow down the chemical reaction. These specimens may be received in pre-filled formalin containers, which the Histopathology laboratory provides, or in generic specimen cups to which 10% formalin has been added. The later must be labeled with a 10% formalin hazard label. If the volume of fixative does not cover the sample, or the sample is squeezed into a container that does not allow enough formalin, contact the resident to add more formalin or transfer to a larger container. The volume of fixative should be at least two times that of the specimen.)
/K [23]
/Pg 118 0 R
/S /H4
/T (Anything received in 10% neutral buffered formalin can be held at room temperature until grossed by the resident. Refrigeration \(2-80C\) is not needed and should be avoided so as not to slow down the chemical reaction. These specimens may be received in pre-filled formalin containers, which the Histopathology laboratory provides, or in generic specimen cups to which 10% formalin has been added. The later must be labeled with a 10% formalin hazard label. If the volume of fixative does not cover the sample, or the sample is squeezed into a container that does not allow enough formalin, contact the resident to add more formalin or transfer to a larger container. The volume of fixative should be at least two times that of the specimen.)
/Type /StructElem
