4727 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Procedure must be carried out exclusively in clean room identified for donning procedure. No exposed skin or hair of the laboratory personnel should be visible at the conclusion of the donning process.)
/K [13]
/P 7260 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4728 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (The laboratory personnel must have adequate liquid or drinks in order to avoid interruption of sample collection due to thirst or dehydration. PPE requires a tight fitting therefore; one may lose fluid due to perspiration and as a result dehydration may occur.)
/K [14]
/P 7261 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4729 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Remove Personal Clothing and Items and Change into surgical scrubs \(or disposable garments\). No personal items \(e.g., jewellery, watches, cell phones, pagers, pens\) should be brought into patient room.)
/K [15]
/P 7262 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4730 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Visually inspect the PPE to be worn to ensure it is in serviceable condition, all required PPE and supplies are available, and that the sizes selected are correct for the laboratory personnel.)
/K [16]
/P 7263 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4731 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Donning procedure)
/K [17]
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /H3
/T (Donning procedure)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4732 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Perform hand hygiene with hand sanitizer and allow hands to dry before moving to next step.)
/K [18]
/P 7264 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4733 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Wear on first pair of inner gloves.)
/K [19]
/P 7265 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4734 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Put on Apron/gown. Ensure it is large enough to allow unrestricted freedom of movement. Ensure cuffs of inner gloves are tucked under the sleeve of the gown or coverall to prevent skin from getting exposed.)
/K [20]
/P 7266 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4735 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Put on Shoe Covers.)
/K [21]
/P 7267 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4736 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Put on N95 mask. Complete a user seal check.)
/K [22]
/P 7268 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4737 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Put on full-body disposable apron to provide additional protection to the front of the body against exposure to body fluids or excrement from the patient.)
/K [23]
/P 7269 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4738 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Put on second pair of gloves \(with extended cuffs\). Ensure the cuffs are pulled over the sleeves of the gown or coverall.)
/K [24]
/P 7270 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4739 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Put-on full-face shield over the N95 mask to provide additional protection to the front and sides of the face, including skin and eyes.)
/K [25]
/P 7271 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4740 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (The laboratory personnel should be comfortable and able to extend the arms bend at the waist and go through a range of motions to ensure there is enough range of movement while all areas of the body remain covered.)
/K [26]
/P 7272 0 R
/Pg 128 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
