>>
endobj
4756 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (The doffing process is sequence of the procedure that the PPE has been removed properly. Prior to doffing PPE, must remind laboratory personnel to avoid reflexive actions that may put them at risk, such as touching their face.)
/K [13]
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /H4
/T (The doffing process is sequence of the procedure that the PPE has been removed properly. Prior to doffing PPE, must remind laboratory personnel to avoid reflexive actions that may put them at risk, such as touching their face.)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4757 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Doffing procedure)
/K [14]
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /H3
/T (Doffing procedure)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4758 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Inspect the PPE to assess for visible contamination, cuts or tears before starting to remove. If any PPE is visibly contaminated, then disinfect with 70% ethanol.)
/K [15]
/P 7275 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4759 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Disinfect and Remove Outer Gloves without contaminating the inner gloves)
/K [16]
/P 7276 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4760 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Inspect inner gloves for any visible contamination \(Note: Change Inner Gloves in case if there are visible tears and wears. Remove and discard gloves taking care not to contaminate bare hands during removal process and don a new pair of gloves\).)
/K [17]
/P 7277 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4761 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Remove the apron away from the body taking care not to contaminate the Apron/Gown. Roll the apron inside out and discard safely in the bio-hazard box.)
/K [18]
/P 7278 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4762 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Disinfect the inner gloves with 70% ethanol and inspect PPE for any visible contamination.)
/K [19]
/P 7279 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4763 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Remove the full-face shield by tilting the head slightly forward, grabbing the rear strap and pulling it over the head, gently allowing the face shield to fall forward and discard. Avoid touching the front surface of the face shield.)
/K [20]
/P 7280 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4764 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Disinfect the inner gloves with 70% ethanol and remove apron/gown.)
/K [21]
/P 7281 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4765 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Laboratory personnel can seek assistance by the trained observer to remove the apron/gown. Avoid contact of scrubs or disposable garments with outer surface of apron/gown during removal. Pull apron/gown away from body, rolling inside out and touching only the inside of the gown.)
/K [22]
/P 7282 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4766 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (To remove apron/gown, with one hand unzip the suit from inside. Unzip or unfasten completely before rolling down and turning inside out. Avoid contact of scrubs with outer surface of coverall during removal, touching only the inside of the apron/gown.)
/K [23]
/P 7283 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
4767 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/E (Disinfect the inner gloves with 70% ethanol and remove the N95 respirator by tilting the head slightly forward, grasping first the bottom tie or elastic strap, then the top tie or elastic strap, and remove without touching the front of the N95 mask. Discard N95 Respirator.)
/K [24]
/P 7284 0 R
/Pg 129 0 R
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
